---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Frame from '../components/Frame.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { places, courtyardConcept } from '../data/places';
const label = { built: 'In the build', now: 'Being built', next: 'Painted, not built' };
const continents = [
  ['Aethelgard', 'Temperate forests and plains, feudal kingdoms, a church that reads the machine\u2019s interventions as providence. The Spine of the Ancients runs through it. Aethelburg, the Lumina capital, sits at its centre. Havenwood is here.'],
  ['Ferrus Magna', 'Scarred by precursor wars and industrial collapse. Scavenger clans, rust, unstable power. Neo-Veridia is a cyberpunk city built inside a dead factory; Rustwater Fishery catches metal-shelled crabs from coolant-stained water.'],
  ['Sylvandell', 'Jungle that has eaten the ruins. Magic here is biological, a way of talking to a terraforming network nobody remembers building. Krystallos is grown around a crystal lattice; Whisperwind Hermitage hangs in the glowing canopy.'],
  ['The Shifting Wastes', 'Where The System\u2019s grip is weak and reality is unreliable. Zephyr is a city that moves, a fleet of repurposed precursor vehicles that never stops.'],
];
const factions = [
  ['The Lumina Orthodoxy', 'House Lumina, the Keepers of the Lineage and the Silent Guard. Order above all, because order is what The System wants.'],
  ['The Reality Weavers', 'Lord Kaelen Lumina and those who want to merge with the machine rather than serve it.'],
  ['The Thorne Technocracy', 'Duchess Aris Thorne\u2019s engineers on Ferrus Magna, who want the technology without the religion.'],
  ['The Cult of the Whispering Glitch', 'Followers of Valerius, for whom the glitch is revelation.'],
  ['The Sylvan Concord', 'The guardians of Krystallos, in what they believe is harmony with living magic.'],
  ['The Unchained', 'Heretics, Glitched Scions and survivors of correction. Not a house, a network. The ones Kai is most likely to end up among.'],
];
const groups = [
  ['built', 'Anchored', 'Walkable in the packaged build. As real as anything here gets.'],
  ['now', 'Weaving', 'On the same map as the courtyard; the kit is growing to fit them.'],
  ['next', 'Unwritten, but painted', 'Every place starts as a painting. These exist as paintings and wait for the kit. They are not less real for it, only less walkable.'],
] as const;
---
<Base title="World" description="The places of Havenwood, painted before they were built, and the wider world beyond the chapel, which is written and not yet painted.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h1>The world</h1>
        <p>Havenwood is a hill town between a harbour and a chapel on the headland. Each place is painted before it is built, and the build is checked against the painting. Where they differ, the painting is right.</p>
      </div>
      <Frame src={courtyardConcept} alt="Painting of the courtyard: a round teal tree, a tall pale tower, a rose shop with a blue awning, a well, a yellow arch with a clock, and hills behind." label="The town as a painting." caption="The courtyard concept that set the palette: ochre, coral, plaster, violet shadows." sizes="(min-width: 70rem) 78rem, 100vw" widths={[800, 1200, 1600, 2000]} />
    </div>
  </section>

  {groups.map(([status, title, note]) => (
    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2><span class={`state state-${status}`}>{title}</span></h2>
          <p>{note}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="places">
          {places.filter((p) => p.status === status).map((p) => (
            <article class="place" id={p.slug}>
              <figure class="frame">
                <Image src={p.image} alt={p.imageAlt} widths={[600, 1000, 1600]} sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 48rem, 100vw" />
              </figure>
              <div class="place-text">
                <h3>{p.name}</h3>
                <p class="small muted">{p.statusText}</p>
                <p>{p.body}</p>
              </div>
              {p.frames && (
                <div class="frames frames-3 place-frames">
                  {p.frames.map((f) => <Frame src={f.src} alt={f.alt} caption={f.caption} sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 25vw, 100vw" widths={[400, 800, 1200]} />)}
                </div>
              )}
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2><span class="state state-next">Beyond Havenwood</span></h2>
        <p>The wider world as designed in 2025, before the painted look. Four continents, four cities, three outposts and six factions. None of it is painted yet, and a place is not real here until it is painted.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="beyond">
        <div>
          <h3>Continents</h3>
          <dl class="ledger">{continents.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}</dl>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Factions</h3>
          <dl class="ledger">{factions.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}</dl>
          <p class="small muted">Stonehearth Post, in the foothills of the Spine, is a devout village warmed by a hearth that never cools because a precursor plant runs under it, and its Keeper of the Flame is an agent of The System in a robe. That is the pattern for every place: a plain surface, a machine underneath, and someone keeping it quiet.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .places { display: grid; gap: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .place { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.5rem 3rem; align-items: start; }
  .place-frames { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .place h3 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.1rem); margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  @media (max-width: 55rem) { .place { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .beyond { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 2rem 4rem; align-items: start; }
  .beyond h3 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .beyond .ledger > div { grid-template-columns: minmax(7rem, 10rem) 1fr; }
  .beyond .ledger dd { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--fg-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 60rem) { .beyond { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
